.TH ICED\-LIBADWAITA 7 "2026-11-03" "iced-libadwaita 0.1.0" "iced-libadwaita Manual"
.SH NAME
iced\-libadwaita \- libadwaita\-style theme, components and behavior primitives for iced
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
[dependencies]
iced\-libadwaita = { path = "../iced\-libadwaita" }
iced = "0.14"

use iced_libadwaita::prelude::*;
use iced_libadwaita as adw;

let theme = adw::Theme::from_config(&adw::config::Config::load());
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBiced\-libadwaita\fR is a component library for the iced GUI toolkit that follows the GNOME Human Interface Guidelines and libadwaita: a theme, about 150 components, each with a man page generated from its doc comments (\fBiced\-libadwaita\-components\fR(3)), the headless \fIprimitives\fR they are built from, and a shared \fIdesktop configuration\fR (\fBiced\-libadwaita\-desktop.conf\fR(5)) so every application on a desktop behaves the same way.
.PP
The library does not include its gallery. The gallery is a separate crate that depends on the library: \fBcargo run \-p iced\-libadwaita\-gallery\fR.
.SH COMPONENT CONVENTIONS
Every component has the same shape (its constructors, properties, slots and events are on its own page, \fBiced\-libadwaita\-\fIalias\fR(3), indexed by \fBiced\-libadwaita\-components\fR(3)):
.TP
.B Construction
\fBComponent::new(required...)\fR and/or a free function of the same name, \fBaction_row(title)\fR. The required arguments are the minimum to render meaningfully.
.TP
.B Properties
Chained builder methods named after libadwaita's properties: \fB.subtitle(..)\fR, \fB.revealed(..)\fR. Booleans take a value (\fB.flat(true)\fR). \fB.metrics(Metrics)\fR is accepted wherever sizes matter.
.TP
.B Slots
Builder methods that take children: \fB.push(child)\fR, \fB.prefix(..)\fR, \fB.suffix(..)\fR, \fB.pack_start(..)\fR, \fB.top_bar(..)\fR.
.TP
.B Events
\fBon_*\fR callbacks that return the application's message: \fBon_press\fR, \fBon_toggle(bool)\fR, \fBon_input(String)\fR.
.TP
.B Controlled state
Components do not own application state. The application passes \fBactive\fR, \fBexpanded\fR, \fBvalue\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBopen\fR and updates it from the events. Purely visual state (animation progress, hover, an open popover) lives inside the component.
.TP
.B Conversion
Every component implements \fBInto<Element>\fR, so they nest freely.
.TP
.B Theme\-driven
Colors, radii, shadows and motion come from the \fBTheme\fR and the desktop configuration, never from the call site.
.PP
A parameter whose default comes from the toolkit or the configuration is a plain value that starts at the default, not an \fBOption\fR. A setting that is not on by default is opted into explicitly (for example the surface tint).
.SH THEMING
\fBTheme::from_config(&config)\fR builds the theme the desktop configuration describes: color scheme, accent, density, text scale, shadows, flat header bars, transparency and tint. Building a theme by hand is an opt\-out of the shared desktop behavior.
.TP
.B Colors
The palette is libadwaita's; the semantic layer (\fBwindow\fR, \fBview\fR, \fBheaderbar\fR, \fBcard\fR, \fBsidebar\fR, \fBpopover\fR, \fBdialog\fR and the \fBaccent\fR, \fBdestructive\fR, \fBsuccess\fR, \fBwarning\fR and \fBerror\fR swatches) is derived from it. The accent is one of nine names or any \fB#rrggbb\fR. Text on colored fills is chosen by contrast.
.TP
.B Transparency
\fBTheme::with_transparency(0..1)\fR scales the alpha of every surface background and keeps its color. Tints derived from a surface (hover, press) keep its alpha, so a translucent surface stays translucent in every state. The window must be transparent; client\-side windows are.
.TP
.B Tint
\fBTheme::with_tint(Some(color))\fR mixes a color of its own into the surfaces, its alpha the strength. It is off by default.
.TP
.B Metrics and motion
\fBMetrics\fR holds sizes and radii (default or compact density); animations follow the motion triggers and reduced motion.
.SH WINDOWS, DIALOGS AND SHEETS
A dialog is a modal layer over its parent window, as \fBAdwDialog\fR is: the parent is faded and disabled, and the dialog closes by its close button, Escape or a press outside. The library opens no operating\-system window for a dialog.
.TP
.B Overlay
A layer over a base view, for dialogs and nested windows. The fade (\fBscrim\fR, on by default), modality and \fBclose_on_outside\fR (default true) are the \fBoverlay\fR primitive's rules; a press outside sends \fBon_outside\fR.
.TP
.B Dock
A surface docked against an edge: a footer, a drawer, a bottom sheet. You set its \fBsize\fR across the edge and its \fBlength\fR along it, where it sits (\fBalign\fR), and how far it stands off the edge (\fBmargin\fR; 0 is flush). \fBDockMode::Push\fR makes room for it, as a sidebar does; \fBDockMode::Overlay\fR floats it over a faded base. A hairline border outlines the sides that are not flush.
.TP
.B Separate windows
A window that must outlive the main window is a separate process: \fBwindow::Detached::this_exe()?.arg("\-\-settings").spawn()\fR starts this executable again in its own process group. \fBwindow::Child\fR is for a second window that belongs to the process and goes with it.
.SH FOCUS
\fBFocusScope\fR and \fBfocus_return\fR apply the \fBfocus\fR primitive (after Mantine's use\-focus\-trap, use\-focus\-return and use\-focus\-within): Tab wraps inside a scope, its first focusable widget (or the one named by \fBinitial_focus(id)\fR) takes focus as it appears, and closing a modal gives focus back to what had it. Every \fBOverlay\fR, and so every dialog and docked sheet, is such a scope.
.SH LAYOUT
\fBNavigationSplitView\fR puts a sidebar beside the content when there is room and collapses it to a drawer or a parent page when there is not; the drawer and the in\-flow sidebar share one geometry with \fBDock\fR (\fBprimitives::dock\fR). Breakpoints (\fBsm\fR..\fBxxl\fR) are configurable. \fBMetaComponent\fR chooses among variants of a component by width or by selection.
.SH FORMS
A \fBFormState\fR and a \fBFormSpec\fR decide when a field shows its validity; \fBField\fR draws the label, control and message. Inputs include \fBentry\fR, \fBNumberInput\fR (fixed\-point decimals, never floats), \fBDateInput\fR and \fBDateRangeInput\fR (a calendar popover or dialog), \fBColorInput\fR and \fBColorPicker\fR, \fBAutocomplete\fR and \fBMultiSelect\fR.
.SH PRIMITIVES
The headless half lives in \fBiced_libadwaita::primitives\fR: pure, controlled, unit\-tested logic with no widgets and no look, after Radix UI and Mantine. A component is a primitive plus a look.
.PP
