.SH DESKTOP CONFIGURATION
Desktop\-level behavior is set once per desktop in \fBdesktop.conf\fR and read through \fBiced_libadwaita::config\fR. Lowest to highest priority: built\-in defaults, system files, the user file, and the application's opt\-outs (if the desktop allows them). See \fBiced\-libadwaita\-desktop.conf\fR(5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICED_LIBADWAITA_CONFIG
Path of one file that replaces the system and user files (testing).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
Where the user and system configuration files are looked up.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/iced\-libadwaita/desktop.conf
The user configuration (default \fI~/.config\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/iced\-libadwaita/desktop.conf
System configuration (default \fI/etc/xdg\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
A confirm dialog over the window:
.PP
.nf
let ui = dialog_in_window(
    base,
    AlertDialog::new("Discard changes?").body("They will be lost."),
    Some(Msg::Close),   // a press outside closes it
    adw::window::State::default().radius(&adw::Metrics::default()),
);
.fi
.PP
A bottom sheet over the whole window:
.PP
.nf
Dock::new(base, sheet)
    .open(self.open)
    .mode(DockMode::Overlay)
    .scope(DockScope::Window)
    .on_outside(Msg::Close)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBiced\-libadwaita\-components\fR(3), \fBiced\-libadwaita\-desktop.conf\fR(5)
.PP
The guidance documents in \fIdocs/lib/\fR (choosing a component, layout, theming, windows and menus, motion) and the design rationale in \fIdocs/hig\-inferences/\fR.
